The caller builds a brand-new object literal on every submit attempt — survey.html:357 `var row = { q1_rating: answers.q1, ... }` is inside the submit handler — so `r.response_id` is always undefined and always freshly minted. Contrast the edge function's own claim, beta-ingest/index.ts:155-156: "// Idempotent on the client-generated id, so a retry after a flaky connection can / // never double-count a funnel stage or a survey response." Events satisfy this (event_id is minted once per event and buffered); surveys do not.

